, 4.5-beta1)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta5 - Pop!_OS 22.04 LTS on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600K (16 threads) - 62.56 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf I have joypad inputs assigned to actions Left Joystick Up and/or Left, then these actions are constantly triggered with a raw strength of 1.0 while the game is running, whether a controller is plugged in or not.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n~~Assign new actions, \"move_up\", \"move_left\", \"move_down\", \"move_right\", and then assign them corresponding joypad inputs from the left joystick of an xbox controller or similar.~~ (not required, see comment below)\n\nHave something that reads the inputs to display them out to you when running a scene.\n\nJoypad will be constantly showing as active `move_up` and `move_left`. (or `ui_up` and `ui_left`)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[2025-09-15-joypad-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22349496/2025-09-15-joypad-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type